@startuml correction-pipeline
' End-to-end correction as a lattice that is expanded, reweighted, then
' collapsed. Colour encodes the role of each stage: expand (blue), filter
' (purple), rescore (green), decode (grey).
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/correction-pipeline.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 4 in docs/integration/lling-llang/hierarchical-correction.md §5
' (and the pipeline figure in pipeline-assembly.md).
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Correction pipeline — expand → reweight → collapse

rectangle "**Input**\n\"I saw teh quikc brown fox to the stroe\"" as in #455A64
rectangle "**0. Tokenize → input lattice**\none original edge per token slot" as tok #455A64

rectangle "**1. LevenshteinCorrectionLayer**  (DIM 1)\nautomaton <latex>\cap</latex> Google-Books vocab\nteh→{the·1, ten·1, tea·2}  stroe→{store·1, stroke·2}\nweight = edit distance (Tropical)" as spell #1565C0

' The phonetic dimension (DIM 2) is NOT a downstream stage: the shipped
' HierarchicalCorrector does orthographic edit only. Its principled realization
' fuses edit + articulatory cost into one candidate-generation step — the cascade
' corrector's T_lex (see correction-cascade.puml), never a rescore of the
' candidates edit distance already pre-filtered.
rectangle "**2. CfgFilterLayer**  (DIM 3)\nEarley parse over the lattice —\ndrop / penalise ungrammatical paths\n(active only when a grammar is supplied)" as cfg #6A1B9A

rectangle "**3. LanguageModelLayer**  (DIM 4+5)\n<latex>w' = (1-\lambda) \cdot w + \lambda \cdot (-\log \mathbb{P}(\text{word} \mid \text{context}))</latex>\nMKN n-gram <latex>\oplus</latex> subword embedding" as lm #2E7D32

rectangle "**4. viterbi / nbest**\nshortest-path <latex>\operatorname*{argmax}</latex> over the semiring" as dec #37474F
rectangle "**Output**\n\"I saw the quick brown fox two the store\"" as out #455A64

in --> tok
tok --> spell : EXPAND
spell --> cfg : PRUNE
cfg --> lm : REWEIGHT
lm --> dec : COLLAPSE
dec --> out

note right of spell
  Lattice now encodes a
  **combinatorial space**
  of candidate sentences.
end note
note right of lm
  Context via topological
  forward-DP; the LM prior
  overturns even the
  zero-edit real-word
  error  to → two.
end note
@enduml
